    <div style="max-width:900px; margin:0 auto 70px;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span>What are lab-grown diamonds?</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-plus" style="color:var(--champagne-gold);"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Lab-grown diamonds are authentic, real diamonds grown in advanced laboratories using High-Pressure High-Temperature (HPHT) or Chemical Vapor Deposition (CVD) methods, sharing exact chemical, physical, and optical properties with mined diamonds.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span>Are lab-grown diamonds real diamonds?</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-plus" style="color:var(--champagne-gold);"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes! The FTC certifies that lab-grown diamonds are 100% genuine diamonds with identical hardness (10 on Mohs scale), sparkle, and GIA/IGI certification.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span>What is the difference between lab-grown and natural diamonds?</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-plus" style="color:var(--champagne-gold);"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          The only difference is origin. Mined diamonds come from deep beneath the earth, whereas lab-grown diamonds are ethically created in a laboratory, offering 40-70% greater value and zero environmental disruption.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span>Do your diamonds come with certification?</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-plus" style="color:var(--champagne-gold);"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Every SAT Jewel gemstone of 0.50 ct and above comes with an official GIA or IGI grading report verifying its Cut, Clarity, Color, and Carat weight.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span>What does VVS quality mean?</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-plus" style="color:var(--champagne-gold);"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          VVS stands for "Very Very Slightly Included", indicating microscopic inclusions that are virtually impossible to see under 10x magnification, guaranteeing supreme optical clarity.
        </div>
      </div>
